    description: "FILED BY OWNER RULING 2026-11-17; NOT PART OF THE SMART-TEST BUILD. The fast-smart-test plan counts a pre-PR cycle as the mypy gate, the slice and the tests. It leaves out the regeneration of docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, which runs `hypergumbo run` on the repository (scripts/generate-architecture) and takes 6 minutes or more. In the last 60 commits on dev (2026-11-17, d0e00a83c) there are 12 \"ci: test manifest\" commits and 8 \"regenerate ARCHITECTURE.md\" commits. Once smart-test selects from a stored graph this is the largest fixed cost of a pre-PR cycle.\n\nTO FIND OUT. What triggers it (a 30-commit gate and a module-count gate are noted in the lab notebook); how much of the time is the analysis; whether it can read the analysis smart-test's detached rebuild already produced.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The measured time and its parts; then either a change that cuts it, with the new time, or the reason it cannot be cut.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 35d0
